# The SPA fallback, scoped to the one route that needs it.
#
# `/r/<code>` is an invitation link: `Main.kt` reads `window.location.pathname` before the
# first composition and seats the visitor at that room. Pages has to answer those paths with
# the shell, or an invitation 404s.
#
# **Scoped on purpose, and this is the important line in the file.** The obvious rule is
# `/* /index.html 200`, and it is a trap this project has already been bitten by: with it, a
# missing asset is answered with `index.html` — 200, `text/html` — so a browser that asked
# for a script gets a web page and a cache rule then keeps it for a year (see
# docs/kotlin/README.md §6c). Restricted to `/r/`, a missing `composeApp.js` is a plain 404,
# which is a bug that announces itself instead of one that has to be diagnosed.
/r/* /index.html 200
